{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1542701-no-goth-allowed","id":1542701,"title":"No Goth Allowed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-26T11:04:38-07:00","id":1542701,"title":"No Goth Allowed","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://images2.imgbox.com/0c/ef/qEP9arui_o.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://images2.imgbox.com/0c/ef/qEP9arui_o.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://images2.imgbox.com/0c/ef/qEP9arui_o.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Trapping of the Grave puts a giant \u201cWe are SUPERNATURAL! NOTICE US\u201d neon sign in the circle\u2019s back, Chivalry of Death encourages them to screw with non-death things, not to mentions the whole using tortured souls for their equipments, how do people even makes Abyssal fits in a mixed Circle? They won\u2019t randomly explode with Resonance anymore like Ex2 for acting out-of-Abyssal but I still wouldn\u2019t want one around me! Usually those Spooky Swordsman character in fiction fantasy party only <i>looks</i> creepy, while Abyssal is actually encouraged to be a creepy guy so it gonna be hard to fit them in a circle unless the rest of the member are also huge Deathlord stan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T17:05:15-07:00","id":1542722,"title":"","content":"Other settings only have the creepy people look like it. This is originally a White Wolf IP, though, so when you're a goth, you're a goth all the way, from your first clove cig to your last dreadful day. You can probably disguise trappings of death as being something like a bunch of Sijanese mourners for hire, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T22:23:36-07:00","id":1542748,"title":"","content":"Well of course there's the larceny charm that makes it so the abyssal has disguised the trappings about as well as a lunar's tell. Even if you don't have that there's nothing stopping disguising some of the trappings like working a burial shroud into a cloak so it isn't immediately obvious what it is.<br /> <br /> Then there's cultural claims ie &quot;Yes I am a foreigner with strange and barbaric ways like working the bones of one of my ancestors into my armor to borrow their strength and support.&quot; <i>Gives shifty look while talking in stilted manor. </i><br /> <br /> I'd need to check chivalry again to recall how those work this time around. Though soulsteel artifacts don't usually stand out more than most other artifacts would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T23:43:27-07:00","id":1542755,"title":"","content":"Reminder: By default, trappings can be as hard as difficulty 5 to notice.<br /> <br /> (Also, Jen's doing a bit here, because he's been around for 3e Abyssals discussion and knows some of the proposed solutions.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T01:23:38-07:00","id":1542756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1542701-no-goth-allowed?p=1542722#post1542722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other settings only have the creepy people look like it. This is originally a White Wolf IP, though, so when you're a goth, you're a goth all the way, from your first clove cig to your last dreadful day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it\u2019s why the Dusk in my party atm is actually just a Dawn with makeup \ud83e\udd2d <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1542701-no-goth-allowed?p=1542748#post1542748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well of course there's the larceny charm that makes it so the abyssal has disguised the trappings about as well as a lunar's tell. Even if you don't have that there's nothing stopping disguising some of the trappings like working a burial shroud into a cloak so it isn't immediately obvious what it is.<br /> <br /> Then there's cultural claims ie &quot;Yes I am a foreigner with strange and barbaric ways like working the bones of one of my ancestors into my armor to borrow their strength and support.&quot; <i>Gives shifty look while talking in stilted manor. </i><br /> <br /> I'd need to check chivalry again to recall how those work this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I guess all those cultural Socialize charms would be good solution to slap away \u201cLook at this weird freak, let kill them\u201d, though I think the solar can only use them on himself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though soulsteel artifacts don't usually stand out more than most other artifacts would. </div> </div> </div>The jig is up once my Zenith turns on his wizard eyes and takes one look at those equipments though, then comes the banhammer\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T11:28:51-07:00","id":1542787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1542701-no-goth-allowed?p=1542756#post1542756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah I guess all those cultural Socialize charms would be good solution to slap away \u201cLook at this weird freak, let kill them\u201d, though I think the solar can only use them on himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure the abyssal has ones that can do the trick as well, and of course there's always just always just the natural ability to lie like a dog.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1542701-no-goth-allowed?p=1542756#post1542756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The jig is up once my Zenith turns on his wizard eyes and takes one look at those equipments though, then comes the banhammer\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Dragonblood who also use soul steel because artifacts are a pain to make, lunars also being resonant, liminals existing, and the joys of the fact that attuning an artifact you're not resonant to in this edition just means you can't access its super powers as easily or effectively if it has them. (As opposed to 2e when you had to make a check and took freaking damage trying to attune out of type materials.) <br /> <br /> Besides Zenith breaks out the banhammer I get to break out the goremaul of peace. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T12:06:37-07:00","id":1542791,"title":"","content":"Being hard to fit in should be taken as a source of tension to add to the experience rather than a reason not to do it. It all depends on what they actually have in common that might push them to try and overcome that friction.<br /> <br /> The rest of the circle doesn't have to be on board with the Deathlords until after maybe the Abyssal has spent time trying to bring them around to the merits of that. Meanwhile, anybody in the circle who cares might convinve the Deathknight that it would be nice to ease the suffering of their Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T21:52:38-07:00","id":1542992,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who remembers being so goth after watching the Matrix as a teen in 1999, that they wore sunglasses while getting milk out of the fridge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T21:59:46-07:00","id":1542993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1542701-no-goth-allowed?p=1542992#post1542992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who remembers being so goth after watching the Matrix as a teen in 1999, that they wore sunglasses while getting milk out of the fridge?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Werewolf player, goth was quickly processed out of my system. It's like drinking sugar alcohols, see...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T10:12:49-07:00","id":1543009,"title":"","content":"Funny thing is, whenever I try to think about what an Abyssal in a modern context would look like, I don't see somebody in goth fashion, I see them wearing a crisp black suit.<br /> <br /> The uncanny element comes from the point that they're wearing that suit in a lot of circumstances where it would seem inappropriate, and the dawning realisation that it would be the particular style that a person might be buried in.<br /> <br /> That and, in my mind, there would be something unsettling about a person being dressed so formally while carrying out actions of the chivalry of death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T10:24:24-07:00","id":1543012,"title":"","content":"Out of the original signature circle, the Disciple would probably go that route, and the Physician might when he isn't... working. Everyone else gets off on freaking the mundanes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T14:44:32-07:00","id":1543028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1542701-no-goth-allowed?p=1543009#post1543009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny thing is, whenever I try to think about what an Abyssal in a modern context would look like, I don't see somebody in goth fashion, I see them wearing a crisp black suit.<br /> <br /> The uncanny element comes from the point that they're wearing that suit in a lot of circumstances where it would seem inappropriate, and the dawning realisation that it would be the particular style that a person might be buried in.<br /> <br /> That and, in my mind, there would be something unsettling about a person being dressed so formally while carrying out actions of the chivalry of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh that actually would be funny. Modern abyssal being able to work the outfit they would wear for burial into the attire and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T09:12:10-08:00","id":1545791,"title":"","content":"Did I miss something and Abyssals got released for Ex3 or are we talking Essence edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T11:38:40-08:00","id":1545797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1542701-no-goth-allowed?p=1545791#post1545791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss something and Abyssals got released for Ex3 or are we talking Essence edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Backers from the crowdfunding last year have access to the initial manuscript, so it's not that the whole book was released, but lots of people have access to the likely written content of Sworn to the Grave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T05:01:13-08:00","id":1547106,"title":"","content":"In my experience the problem isn't so much with a lone Abyssal in a mixed circle as usually the player who actively chose to play an Abyssal has put enough thought into their whole demeanour and aesthetic that it'll qualify as trappings of death. <br /> <br /> Where I have seen an issue is when it's an Abyssals game and there were two factors I observed at play there-<br /> <br /> -They didn't necessarily want to play an Abyssal, they're playing an Abyssal because it was functionally a choice between playing an Abyssal or not playing Exalted.<br /> <br /> -They wanted to stand out, the problem with having 3-5 people from the same friend group playing Abyssals is that their sense of style for cool goth villains might overlap with someone whose doing it better. Ever since 1st edition I've seen people express a preference for Day and Moonshadow Castes who seem normal by the standards of their circlemates but are anything but.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}